Z||000000||Rex||05-14-2001||04:50 PM||||What type of instrument is used for retrieving codes and what do they cost.||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroLisa||05-14-2001||04:59 PM||||there is a little code key that you can get from focoa, and probably other places (maybe a dealer) I have 2 of them laying around, but they are at my house in NC||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||05-14-2001||05:00 PM||||You can retrieve the codes with a paperclip.  Simply short out the two pins on the ALDL connector located behind the cigarette lighter plate while the ignition is on but the engine is not running.  The check engine light will blink the series of stored codes.<P>Cost - next to nothing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tryxalon||05-14-2001||05:45 PM||||And if your "check engine" light does not work?? <P>I've checked fuses, grounds, bulbs, connection ... only thing I haven't done is wire in alternate bulb off of ECM harness. <P>Or is there another way?? <P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierospeeder||05-14-2001||05:59 PM||||A PAPER CLIP<P><BR>Your lucky the fiero doesn't have ABS brakes or computerized suspension.  Then you have to get those special tools.<P>There are computers to check what the real time info is on all the sensors which will run around 100 dollars.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Pontiaddict||05-14-2001||07:57 PM||||Actually on early ABS systems, you could check for codes in a similar manner as the computer. Ground out the corresponding terminal on the ALDL connector and wait for the codes on the ABS warnng light.<BR>There might be a similar terminal on the ALDL that would allow you to do the same thing with an computer controlled suspension. I haven't had much experience with that.||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroJoe||05-14-2001||09:12 PM||||Here's a good link to follow that'll explain how to interpret the codes:<BR> <A HREF="http://home.att.net/~fieroshadow/fierohelp/aldl.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.att.net/~fieroshadow/fierohelp/aldl.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000007||Philphine||05-14-2001||10:00 PM||||autozone will give you one free (a key, not a scanner) with a book to interpret the codes.||||reg||1
Z||000008||85Josh||05-14-2001||11:02 PM||||Beat me to it, Phil, I was going to say my AutoZone gave me a handful.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
Z||000009||Ed||05-14-2001||11:14 PM||||My Dodge Caravan is even simpler than my Fiero.  Just cycle the ignition key three times and the codes show up. ||||reg||1
